BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Media School
DTSTART:20261117T223000Z
DTEND:20261117T233000Z
LOCATION:IMU Whittenberger Auditorium
SUMMARY:Advance Screening of The Hunger Games: Sunrise on the Reaping
DESCRIPTION:A free "End the Stigma" festival will begin at 7:30 p.m. and 
 feature mental health learning stations\, activities\, giveaways\, inform
 ation about campus programs and snacks. The event will take place at the 
 IMU Whittenberger Auditorium.  The event is sponsored by University Bring
  Change to Mind (UBC2M)\, a student-centered college program associated w
 ith Bring Change to Mind\, the nonprofit founded by Glenn Close and her f
 amily. Through student-led efforts\, UBC2M encourages connection and open
  conversations about mental health while working to reduce stigma surroun
 ding mental illness. The program is housed in IU's Irsay Institute\, whic
 h conducts research on mental health\, addiction and other health care is
 sues.  From acclaimed director Francis Lawrence\, THE HUNGER GAMES: SUNRI
 SE ON THE REAPING follows sixteen-year-old Haymitch Abernathy (Joseph Zad
 a) from District 12\, beginning on the morning of the reaping for the 50t
 h Annual Hunger Games\, also known as the Second Quarter Quell\, the bigg
 est Games yet with twice as many tributes.  Set in the world of Panem 24 
 years before the events of The Hunger Games\, the story follows Haymitch 
 into the arena\, where he forms an unlikely alliance with fellow tribute 
 Maysilee Donner (Mckenna Grace) and joins a coalition determined to chall
 enge the Capitol's control under President Snow (Ralph Fiennes). As the c
 ompetition unfolds\, Haymitch risks everything to take down the Games fro
 m within the arena\, setting in motion the rebellion that will change Pan
 em forever.  Tickets are free\, however\, there will be opportunities to 
 donate if desired. Proceeds will support student mental health events and
  opportunities on campus.&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  A free "End the Stigma" festival will b
 egin at 7:30 p.m. and feature mental health learning stations\, activitie
 s\, giveaways\, information about campus programs and snacks. The event w
 ill take place at the IMU Whittenberger Auditorium.</p><p>  The event is 
 sponsored by University Bring Change to Mind (UBC2M)\, a student-centered
  college program associated with Bring Change to Mind\, the nonprofit fou
 nded by Glenn Close and her family. Through student-led efforts\, UBC2M e
 ncourages connection and open conversations about mental health while wor
 king to reduce stigma surrounding mental illness. The program is housed i
 n IU's Irsay Institute\, which conducts research on mental health\, addic
 tion and other health care issues.</p><p>  From acclaimed director Franci
 s Lawrence\, <em>THE HUNGER GAMES: SUNRISE ON THE REAPING</em> follows si
 xteen-year-old Haymitch Abernathy (Joseph Zada) from District 12\, beginn
 ing on the morning of the reaping for the 50th Annual Hunger Games\, also
  known as the Second Quarter Quell\, the biggest Games yet with twice as 
 many tributes.</p><p>  Set in the world of Panem 24 years before the even
 ts of <em>The Hunger Games</em>\, the story follows Haymitch into the are
 na\, where he forms an unlikely alliance with fellow tribute Maysilee Don
 ner (Mckenna Grace) and joins a coalition determined to challenge the Cap
 itol's control under President Snow (Ralph Fiennes). As the competition u
 nfolds\, Haymitch risks everything to take down the Games from within the
  arena\, setting in motion the rebellion that will change Panem forever.<
 /p><p>  Tickets are free\, however\, there will be opportunities to donat
 e if desired. Proceeds will support student mental health events and oppo
 rtunities on campus.&#160\;</p>
